{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Small-twist expansion of the FSoV scalar product — gl(4) L=2\n\nTakes the finished scalar product of `Clean/SU4_SoV_ScalarProduct_L2.wb` and switches the twist off\nalong a **unimodular** ray, `z1 z2 z3 z4 = 1` exactly, `phi1+phi2+phi3+phi4 = 0`.\n\nStep 1 (this notebook's first goal): does **orthogonality survive the expansion**, i.e. is\n`det M^{AB}` still zero for `A != B` order by order in the twist, and is `det M^{AA}` still nonzero\nat its own leading order?\n\nThe machinery is not re-derived: cell 2 loads the Clean notebook's code cells verbatim.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 0. Load the validated machinery from the Clean notebook (code cells 1,2,3,5 only:\n       twist/transfer matrices, TwistedSolve, Q-functions/operators, scalar product).\n       Cells 4 and 6 there are the CHECKS and are deliberately not run.\n\n       TRAP: ToExpression on a raw cell string splits at every newline that ends a complete\n       expression, so a definition whose RHS is continued on the next line (BaxRes) is silently\n       truncated -- the same failure mode recorded for this notebook's front end. joinCont glues\n       a continuation line (one starting with a binary operator) back onto its predecessor.\n       Verified below: BaxRes must depend on the tc. ---- *)\nClearAll[cleanPath, cleanCode, joinCont];\ncleanPath = \"/home/paul/git_projects/gaudin-CG/Paul/Mathematica/XXX/Clean/SU4_SoV_ScalarProduct_L2.wb\";\njoinCont[s_] := StringReplace[s, RegularExpression[\"\\\\n[ \\\\t]*([-+*/])\"] -> \" $1\"];\ncleanCode = joinCont[#[\"value\"]] & /@ Select[Import[cleanPath, \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"], #[\"kind\"] == 2 &];\nToExpression /@ cleanCode[[{1, 2, 3, 5}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"961318\" data-output-id=\"101\" data-out-n=\"9\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"1\" data-sub-start=\"13\" data-sub-end=\"13\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[9]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-line-broken=\"1\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:6em;vertical-align:-2.75em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-r\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.75em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.84em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.75em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:3.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-5.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">1. twist and transfer matrices loaded</span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.91em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">2. solver loaded; unimodular?</span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">True</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">3. Q-functions and operators loaded</span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-0.91em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">4. scalar product loaded</span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0